 "result": "I wrote a `Dockerfile`, a `docker-entrypoint.sh` and a `.dockerignore` in the repository root. I couldn't build or run the image here, so none of it has been tested. I didn't modify any existing files.\n\n**How the image works**\n- **Web UI build:** the first stage builds the Next.js UI with `npm ci` and `npm run build`. That produces a static export, which is copied into `web_dist/`, the directory the backend serves it from.\n- **Runtime image:** the second stage is `python:3.13-slim`, matching `requires-python >=3.13`. It installs the Python dependencies with `uv sync --frozen --no-dev` from `uv.lock`.\n- **System packages:** it adds `chromium` and `nodejs`/`npm` for the Grok browser bridge, plus `openssl` for encrypted backups and `git` for the git storage backend.\n- **Browser bridge:** the backend only accepts a loopback bridge URL (default `http://127.0.0.1:3080`), so the bridge has to run in the same container. `docker-entrypoint.sh` starts it in the background with `node services/browser_bridge/server.js`. It then runs `python main.py` as the main process, listening on port 83 (`PORT`). Set `DISABLE_BROWSER_BRIDGE=1` to skip the bridge.\n- **Configuration:** `.env.example` documents settings like `LOGIN_SECRET`, `STORAGE_BACKEND` and `PROXY_URL`. Pass them with `-e` or `--env-file`. `/app/data` is declared as a volume for persistence.\n\n**Things to know**\n- `pyproject.toml` and `uv.lock` point at the Aliyun PyPI mirror, which may be slow outside China. I left that alone because I can't edit those files.\n- The container runs as root, because the default port 83 is privileged and the bridge launches Chromium with `--no-sandbox`.\n\n**Example**\n```\ndocker build -t webchat2api .\ndocker run -p 83:83 -e LOGIN_SECRET=change-me -v $(pwd)/data:/app/data webchat2api\n```\n\n**Files created**\n- `Dockerfile`\n- `docker-entrypoint.sh`\n- `.dockerignore`",
